{"resource":{"id":"react-complete-tutorial","title":"React.js — Complete Tutorial","category":"Web Development","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"44 min","pages":67,"lastUpdated":"September 2026","tags":["Web Development","React","Hooks"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A complete end-to-end React.js tutorial — fundamentals, hooks, Context API, routing, forms, API integration, performance, custom hooks, auth, testing, deployment, and React 19 patterns."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Fundamentals"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Components & JSX"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. State Management"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Hooks in Depth"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Context API"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. React Router"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Forms & Validation"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. API Integration"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Performance Optimization"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Custom Hooks"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Authentication"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Testing"},{"id":"s13","label":"13. Deployment"},{"id":"s14","label":"14. React 19 Best Practices"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"React.js — Beginner Guide","tag":"Web Development","time":"12 min"},{"title":"React.js — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Web Development","time":"5 min"},{"title":"React.js — Interview Questions","tag":"Web Development","time":"34 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Build production React applications from scratch to deployment.</li>\n          <li>Master hooks, Context, routing, forms, and API integration.</li>\n          <li>Optimize performance, write custom hooks, and add authentication.</li>\n          <li>Write tests and ship using modern deployment platforms.</li>\n          <li>Apply React 19 patterns like Actions, useOptimistic, and Server Components.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Fundamentals</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React is a declarative library. You describe UI as a function of state, and React reconciles the virtual DOM into real DOM updates.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Mental model</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">UI = f(state). Change state, React re-renders.</div></div></div></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — React reconciliation: virtual DOM diff produces minimal real DOM patches.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Components &amp; JSX</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function Button({ label, onClick }) {\n  return &lt;button onClick={onClick}&gt;{label}&lt;/button&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Function components are the default. JSX compiles to <code>React.createElement</code> calls at build time.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. State Management</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Start with <code>useState</code>. Scale up with <code>useReducer</code> for complex transitions, and Context or Zustand/Redux for cross-tree state.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducer, initialState);</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Hooks in Depth</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><code>useState</code> — local state</li>\n          <li><code>useEffect</code> — side effects after render</li>\n          <li><code>useRef</code> — mutable value, DOM handle</li>\n          <li><code>useMemo</code> / <code>useCallback</code> — memoization</li>\n          <li><code>useLayoutEffect</code> — synchronous DOM measurement</li>\n          <li><code>useTransition</code> / <code>useDeferredValue</code> — concurrent UI</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Context API</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const ThemeContext = createContext(&quot;light&quot;);\nfunction App() {\n  return &lt;ThemeContext.Provider value=&quot;dark&quot;&gt;&lt;Toolbar /&gt;&lt;/ThemeContext.Provider&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. React Router</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>import { BrowserRouter, Routes, Route } from &quot;react-router-dom&quot;;\n&lt;BrowserRouter&gt;\n  &lt;Routes&gt;\n    &lt;Route path=&quot;/&quot; element={&lt;Home /&gt;} /&gt;\n    &lt;Route path=&quot;/posts/:id&quot; element={&lt;Post /&gt;} /&gt;\n  &lt;/Routes&gt;\n&lt;/BrowserRouter&gt;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Forms &amp; Validation</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React Hook Form + Zod is the modern combo — minimal re-renders, type-safe schemas.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const { register, handleSubmit } = useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) });</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. API Integration</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const { data, isLoading } = useQuery({\n  queryKey: [&quot;users&quot;],\n  queryFn: () =&gt; fetch(&quot;/api/users&quot;).then((r) =&gt; r.json()),\n});</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Performance Optimization</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><code>React.memo</code> for expensive pure components.</li>\n          <li>Code-split with <code>React.lazy</code> + Suspense.</li>\n          <li>Virtualize long lists with react-window.</li>\n          <li>Profile with React DevTools.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Profiling flow: measure, isolate hotspots, memoize, verify.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Custom Hooks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function useLocalStorage(key, initial) {\n  const [v, setV] = useState(() =&gt; JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) ?? &quot;null&quot;) ?? initial);\n  useEffect(() =&gt; localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(v)), [key, v]);\n  return [v, setV];\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Authentication</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Store JWTs in httpOnly cookies. Wrap protected routes in an auth guard component. Refresh tokens silently on 401.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>import { render, screen } from &quot;@testing-library/react&quot;;\ntest(&quot;renders&quot;, () =&gt; {\n  render(&lt;Greeting name=&quot;Ada&quot; /&gt;);\n  expect(screen.getByText(/Ada/)).toBeInTheDocument();\n});</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">13. Deployment</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Build with <code>vite build</code> and deploy to Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, or any static host. Add proper SPA fallback routing.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">14. React 19 Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Use Actions for async mutations with built-in pending/error state.</li>\n          <li><code>useOptimistic</code> for instant UI feedback.</li>\n          <li>Server Components for zero-JS static content.</li>\n          <li>The new <code>use()</code> hook to unwrap promises and context.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React scales from a single component to enterprise apps. Master hooks, data-fetching, and performance to ship confidently.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Redux or Context?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Context for low-frequency global state; Zustand or Redux Toolkit for high-frequency updates.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>CSS-in-JS or Tailwind?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Tailwind for speed; CSS Modules or vanilla-extract for type-safe design systems.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Verify APIs against the latest React documentation.</p>\n      </div></section>"}